      Merge OSS PR 11928 into Proprietary (#7157)
      
      What:
      Import OSS PR https://github.com/semgrep/semgrep/pull/11934 into
      proprietary under `OSS/`, preserving the contributor's three commits
      (author Carlos Acosta / @charle-z). Fixes Dockerfile parsing for
      environment-expanded `EXPOSE` ports with TCP/UDP protocols, plus
      changelog and tree-sitter 0.26.3 regeneration.
      
      Why:
      `sync-with-PRO` failed on this already-merged OSS PR because proprietary
      tracks `parser.c` as Git LFS while OSS stores it as a normal blob. We
      need these OSS changes in proprietary so they stay in the Pro↔OSS sync
      loop.
      
      How:
      Applied the OSS commits with `git am --3way --directory=OSS`, resolving
      `parser.c` conflicts by taking the OSS file content and re-adding it
      through LFS. No intentional logic changes beyond the imported OSS
      commits.
      
